    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of everything that happens when you `POST /api/owners`. The endpoint maps to `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, whose body is an explicit chain of policy classes around the save.\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Bean Validation on the request DTO (`OwnerFieldsDto`), runs before the controller body\nTriggered by `@Valid @RequestBody` on the `@Validated` `OwnersApi` interface. Failures \u2192 **400** (`MethodArgumentNotValidException`).\n1. `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words separated by space/`'`/`-`)\n2. `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (same, optional trailing `.`)\n3. `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`, `@Pattern` non-blank\n4. `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`, `@Pattern` non-blank\n5. `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`, `@Pattern` requiring exactly 10 digits\n6. `email` \u2014 optional; `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`\n7. `postcode` \u2014 optional; `@Pattern` exactly 4 digits\n8. `registrationDate` \u2014 optional `LocalDate`; `sharesHousehold` \u2014 optional `Boolean`, no constraints\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Mapping DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity (`OwnerMapper`, MapStruct), with normalization side-effects\n9. `address` normalized: trim, collapse whitespace, uppercase, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`\n10. `telephone` normalized to E.164 (`E164Telephone.toE164`; assumes `+61` and drops a leading `0` if no `+`)\n11. **Validation during mapping:** `OwnerTelephoneLengthPolicy` \u2014 `+61` requires exactly 9 national digits, `+1` exactly 10, else **400** (`InvalidNationalNumberLengthException`)\n12. `email` normalized to lowercase\n\n## Phase 3 \u2014 The controller policy chain (exact order in `addOwner`)\n13. **`OwnerRegistrationDatePolicy`** (side-effect): default `registrationDate` to today if absent, then roll off weekends (Sat\u2192+2, Sun\u2192+1)\n14. **`OwnerDailyLimitPolicy`** (validation): count all owners with the same registrationDate; if \u2265 100 \u2192 **429** (`DailyLimitReachedException`)\n15. **`OwnerCityCapacityPolicy`** (validation): count owners in the same city; if \u2265 50 \u2192 **409** (`CityAtCapacityException`); null city passes\n16. **`OwnerPostcodePolicy`** (validation): if city maps to a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD), postcode must fall in that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099), else **400** (`InvalidPostcodeException`); null postcode or unknown region passes\n17. **`OwnerIdentityPolicy.rejectDuplicateIdentity`**:\n    - side-effect: if `sharesHousehold == true` and another owner matches on normalized lastName+address, set `householdId` (SHA-256-derived 8-byte hex)\n    - validation: build identity key `telephone|email|householdId`; exact match on a different owner \u2192 **409** (`DuplicateIdentityException`)\n18. **`OwnerNamesakePolicy`** (side-effect): set `namesakeCount` = count of existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive)\n19. **`OwnerCustomerCodePolicy`** (side-effect): set `customerCode` = `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, where NNNN = (existing owners in that city) + 1, zero-padded\n\n## Phase 4 \u2014 Persist\n20. **`clinicService.saveOwner`** \u2192 Spring Data JPA `save` (`@Transactional`). On flush, entity-level Bean Validation applies: `firstName`/`lastName`/`address`/`city` `@NotEmpty`, `telephone` `@Pattern ^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$`. `@PrePersist` sets `registrationDate` to today if still null.\n\n## Phase 5 \u2014 After save\n21. **`OwnerAuditPolicy`** (side-effect): emit an `AUDIT` log line (`id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, computed `membershipLevel`)\n22. Map entity \u2192 `OwnerDto`, computing read-only derived fields (`displayName`, `membershipNumber`, `membershipLevel`, `locality`, `bulkSignupWarning`, `contactPreference`, `identityKey`) \u2014 response only, not persisted\n23. Return **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`\n\n## Notes on what does *not* apply\n- **Security / `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(OWNER_ADMIN)\")`**: not enforced by default \u2014 the active profile sets `petclinic.security.enable=false` (permitAll, no method security). It only takes effect under the `security.enable=true` profile.\n- `OwnerTelephonePolicy`, `OwnerEmailPolicy`, `OwnerHouseholdPolicy` still exist (with exception handlers) but are **not called** from the create path \u2014 superseded by `OwnerIdentityPolicy`.\n- No password encoding (owners have none), no events published, no emails/notifications, no interceptors/filters. The only non-persistence side-effect is the audit log line."
  },
